    <md:content-id>m00693</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.1.2: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>270e9dc3-ee97-4af1-8dcc-86350567ca18</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para dir="ltr">The plot below is a scatter plot of mean temperature in July and mean inches of rain per year for a sample of midwestern cities. A line is drawn to fit the data. </para>
<image alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS MEAN TEMPERATURE IN JULY IN DEGREES FAHRENHEIT ON THE X-AXIS AND MEAN RAINFALL PER YEAR IN INCHES ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN INCREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT." class="img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="425" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/afb399190f61185c419bb2d99e3317cec9ab4976" width="450"/><para dir="ltr">Use the line provided to predict the mean number of inches of rain per year for a city that has a mean temperature of 70°F in July. </para></section>
</content>
